# No Opaque IDs In Business Documents

- Never show Firestore IDs, POS sync IDs, random tokens, or sliced IDs in customer/admin-facing labels, PDF filenames, document titles, memos, emails, or print output.
- Use business document numbers instead: `invoiceNumber`, `orderNumber`, `poNumber`, voucher numbers, bill numbers, or generated date-based refs.
- If a legacy document has no human number, show an explicit unnumbered label such as `INV-UNNUMBERED`; do not fall back to `id`, `id.slice(...)`, or `sourceId`.
- Internal database fields like `referenceId`, Firestore doc IDs, and idempotency keys may still store opaque IDs, but they must not become display text.
